Chromium 158.0.8127.18 -> 158.0.8127.28, for the 158.0.8127.18 tarball.

158.0.8127.28 is a tag on the 158 branch (refs/branch-heads/8127@{#1201}) that
has no source tarball (as of 2026-11-06). It adds 356 branch commits to
158.0.8127.18 (#845), 181 of them not PGO/orderfile/AFDO rolls or VERSION increments:
security fixes (MSE, the extension install move, the password auto sign-in toast,
SiteDataClearer, WebShare, PartitionAlloc's purge, service worker teardown, Blink's
animation triggers, scroll snap, nested pseudo-elements, display-locked painting and
video snapshots, and the V8, Skia, ICU, Dawn and ANGLE ones in the 28 "Roll commits
from side projects" and the ICU roll), contextual tasks, composebox/omnibox and new tab
page WebUI changes, PartitionAlloc's ThreadCache overflow churn.

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags: chromium/src
refs/tags/158.0.8127.18..158.0.8127.28 and the dependencies whose DEPS
revision changed (ANGLE, Dawn, DevTools, ICU, Skia, V8, WebRTC), as served by
Gitiles, with scripts/chromium-delta.

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations, CI configuration, PGO/orderfile pointers, submodule pointer
updates, DEPS.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h,
skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h, gpu/webgpu/DAWN_VERSION and
gpu/webgpu/dawn_commit_hash.h; commit 3120c1c0cc1de3dbec7292e4bcb73d3874c21792,
refs/branch-heads/8127@{#1201}). build/util/MINIBRANCH doesn't change.

Checked: applies to the 158.0.8127.18 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
158.0.8127.28; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag (or the dependency's DEPS revision); it adds 12 files and renames
20 (within chrome/browser/resources/omnibox_popup/; the old paths are gone); the
158.0.8127.18 tarball's non-git files are all classified (tarball-generated.py
with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

